    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Third and last of the deliberately-unstatable entries, chosen because it fails for a DIFFERENT reason than the other two and so maps a different edge of the frontier. F:godel-first-incompleteness and F:fol-validity-undecidable are blocked by the absence of reflection alone; this one is blocked by reflection AND by order -- there is no second-order quantification and no cardinality anywhere in the stack, and a 'complete framework for general reasoning' that intends to reach ordinary mathematics eventually has to answer for that. Recorded also as a warning label for the self-extension loop: an `open` fact with `formal.fragment: none` must never be dispatched to a solver, and a consumer that filters only on status will do exactly that.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
